From 6d0d5bc4276b5dc0453ac4869f74bb7dbe070d14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:16:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Product surface: chooser, dual-mode split, selector, collapse
 rules (Phase 5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The five environments get their front door and their pairing.

- Onboarding chooser (§10/§20): "How do you want to program your
  research?" — five numbered cards with tagline, audience and three
  particulars each; opens on a first run of a project (no ?mode=, no
  remembered mode), on ?chooser=1, from the selector's ⓘ, and from ⌘K
  "Choose how to program…"; Escape/backdrop/"Keep Studio" dismiss and
  remember. The sandbox is exempt unless asked — it is scratch, and 48
  browser suites open it expecting the Questions panel unobstructed.
- Dual-mode split (§15): a {mode, split} pair in the mode layer with
  ?split= in the URL and memory; nextPair swaps when the partner becomes
  primary, refuses a mode with itself, drops an unavailable partner.
  SplitCenter renders two panes from one ModeRenderer table (the single
  view uses the same table), each with a head (index, name, tagline,
  swap, close), a draggable remembered ratio; the outer property panel
  steps aside. Both panes are views of the one store, so an edit in Grid
  is on the Flow canvas on the same render and a node clicked in Flow is
  the row selected in Grid — nothing was written to make that so.
  Commands split.<mode>, split.off, mode.choose. Folds to the primary
  below 1100px (matchMedia) and comes back when the window widens.
- Selector (§11): numbered ranges (01 Studio … 05 Intelligent), the
  paired mode marked, a Split menu, a Focus switch wired to the same
  view-level flag every shell reads, and the ⓘ.
- Visual language (§11): a --ide-* token extension read only by the mode
  chrome and the .sg/.ar/.fc/.iq shells — type ramp, mono identifiers,
  one pane-head height, hairlines, status colours. Nothing the respondent
  renderer or an existing panel reads changed.
- Collapse rules (§17): container queries on the split pane and the
  centre column — Flow/Intelligent/Architect inspectors fold under 960px,
  Architect's map under 640px; the mode bar folds its labels, then its
  indexes, then its tools.
- Flow: the first fit used a guessed 1200×700 before the canvas was
  measured (wrong in a pane); size starts at 0×0 and fit waits.
- Tests: lib (nextPair/resolveInitialSplit/withSplitInUrl/shouldShowChooser,
  split + chooser commands; mutation-checked), scripts/product-surface-
  test.mjs (31 checks). Foundation, Grid, Architect, Flow, Intelligent and
  eight older shell suites still pass.

